\title{Adding a new math function to VerifiedLibc}
\taxon{Note}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{antigravity}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{architecture}
\tag{guide}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Each verified LLVM libc math function lives at the top level of \code{\verb~|LibcMath/~}: an entry module \code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>.lean~} and a directory \code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/~} with a fixed structure. \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf.lean~} and \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf/~} are the worked example, and \code{\verb~|templates/FunctionTemplate/~} is a copyable skeleton.}

\p{Proofs are directed by numerical analysis, not exhaustive enumeration ([dec-US4Q](dec-US4Q)). Shared building blocks live under \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/~} so a new function plugs into the same range-reduction, rounding-transfer, and Chebyshev SLZ Table Maker's Dilemma machinery instead of rebuilding it.}

\subtree[note-adding-a-function-layout]{
\title{Directory shape}

\p{Copy \code{\verb~|templates/FunctionTemplate/~} to \code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/~} and \code{\verb~|templates/FunctionTemplate.lean~} to \code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>.lean~}, replacing \code{\verb~|Fn~} / \code{\verb~|fn~} with your function name (for example, \code{\verb~|Exp2f~} / \code{\verb~|exp2f~}):}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>.lean~} — entry point: imports the short paths and main path, states and proves the top-level theorem, and carries \code{\verb~|#guard_msgs in #print axioms~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/Generated/~} — plans emitted by \code{\verb~|ast2lean~}; never edited by hand and never mixed with hand-written files.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/Plans.lean~} — hand-written catalogue collecting \code{\verb~|allPlans~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/Statement.lean~} — \code{\verb~|CorrectlyRounded~} statements for the extracted evaluation plans.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/ShortPaths/{Exec,Ranges}.lean~} — symbolic evaluation and whole-range correctness for zeros, infinities, NaNs, tiny arguments, overflow, and underflow.}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/MainPath/~} — one file per numerical-analysis step (range reduction and UB-freedom, real polynomial approximation, floating-point Horner evaluation error, table bounds, combined value error, isolated pointwise exceptions, and TMD rounding clearance; generated certificate chunks stay isolated under \code{\verb~|MainPath/Tmd/Certs/~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/Examples.lean~} — worked evaluations and \code{\verb~|Libc.Diag~} checks compiled as part of \code{\verb~|lake build~}.}
}
}

\subtree[note-adding-a-function-steps]{
\title{Step-by-step workflow}

\ol{
\li{\strong{Add the specification.} If the mathematical specification is not yet in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Framework/Specs.lean~}, add \code{\verb~|Spec.<fn>~} following ISO C23 Annex F.10.}
\li{\strong{Extract the plans with \code{\verb~|ast2lean~}.} Write an extraction script modelled on \code{\verb~|extract/extract-expf-plans.sh~} that emits each build plan into \code{\verb~|LibcMath/<Function>/Generated/~} with \code{\verb~|--namespace=LibcMath.<Function>.Generated.<Plan>~}. Add \code{\verb~|Plans.lean~} next to \code{\verb~|Generated/~} collecting \code{\verb~|allPlans~}.}
\li{\strong{Write the statement.} In \code{\verb~|Statement.lean~}, define \code{\verb~|<Function>CorrectlyRounded~} against \code{\verb~|Spec.<fn>~} and \code{\verb~|cModes~} (or \code{\verb~|{.nearest}~} for RN-only plans).}
\li{\strong{Prove the short paths for whole ranges.} Add closed-form range theorems for the real function under \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/~} (modelled on \code{\verb~|Analysis/ExpRanges.lean~}). Evaluate the extracted kernel symbolically in \code{\verb~|ShortPaths/Exec.lean~} and join the ranges with \code{\verb~|HoldsOnBits.append~} in \code{\verb~|ShortPaths/Ranges.lean~}.}
\li{\strong{Decompose the main path into analytical steps.} Create one file per step under \code{\verb~|MainPath/~}:
  \ul{
  \li{\strong{Range reduction & UB-freedom} (\code{\verb~|MainPath/RangeReduction.lean~}): reuse \code{\verb~|Analysis/RangeReduction.lean~} for exact power-of-two scaling, \code{\verb~|genericNearestInt~}, Sterbenz subtraction, widening casts, and checked \code{\verb~|fptosi?~} / \code{\verb~|sadd?~} / table bounds. Note any isolated rounding edge cases (like \code{\verb~|0x3B7FFFFF~} and \code{\verb~|0xBB7FFFFF~} in \code{\verb~|expf~}) early.}
  \li{\strong{Real polynomial bound} (\code{\verb~|MainPath/Polynomial.lean~}): bound \code{\verb~||poly r - f r|~} on the reduced interval via FloatLib's \code{\verb~|interval~} tactic and Taylor bounds.}
  \li{\strong{Evaluation & table error} (\code{\verb~|MainPath/HornerError.lean~}, \code{\verb~|TableBounds.lean~}, \code{\verb~|ProductError.lean~}): reuse \code{\verb~|Analysis/Horner.lean~} (\code{\verb~|hornerStep_binary64~}, \code{\verb~|mul_rel_bounds~}, \code{\verb~|round_rel_bounds~}) to bound floating-point rounding across all four C modes, and certify lookup tables via rational enclosures + \code{\verb~|decide +kernel~}.}
  \li{\strong{Rounding transfer & TMD} (\code{\verb~|MainPath/PointwiseExceptions.lean~}, \code{\verb~|MainPath/Tmd/~}): plug the value error bound \code{\verb~|ε~} into the shared \code{\verb~|Analysis/RoundingTransfer.lean~} (\code{\verb~|roundReal_eq_of_awayFromGrid~}) and \code{\verb~|Analysis/ChebTmd.lean~} (pure-\code{\verb~|Nat~} always-odd Chebyshev SLZ verifier), discharging the finite list of hard-to-round inputs individually via a proved-sound oracle + \code{\verb~|decide +kernel~}.}
  }
  Any step not yet proved stays a named lemma ending in \code{\verb~|sorry~} with a \code{\verb~|/-- **Open.** ... -/~} docstring, never a hypothesis of the top-level theorem. Run \code{\verb~|python3 scripts/check-open.py --update~} to keep \code{\verb~|OPEN.md~} in sync.}
\li{\strong{Add examples, imports, and differential tests.} Wire \code{\verb~|LibcMath.<Function>~} into \code{\verb~|LibcMath.lean~}, add \code{\verb~|Examples.lean~}, register the kernel in \code{\verb~|Testing/Target.lean~} for \code{\verb~|checkrange~}, and add a differential test script modelled on \code{\verb~|scripts/difftest-expf.sh~}. Verify \code{\verb~|lake build~}, \code{\verb~|python3 scripts/check-open.py~}, \code{\verb~|bash extract/test/run_tests.sh~}, and \code{\verb~|journal-build~}.}
}
}
